  { q: 'Is decision intelligence just AI?', a: 'No. AI and machine learning can support parts of it, such as forecasting or suggesting options, but decision intelligence is mainly about how decisions are framed, informed, owned and evaluated. Much of it can be done with clear models, good data and discipline.' },
  { q: 'How is decision intelligence different from business intelligence?', a: 'Business intelligence produces information: reports, dashboards and analyses. Decision intelligence starts from the decision and works backwards to the information, assumptions and owners it needs, then records what was decided and checks whether it worked.' },
  { q: 'What is a decision model?', a: 'A structured description of a decision: the options available, the outcomes it is meant to affect, the factors that link actions to outcomes, the evidence for each link, and who is accountable. It makes reasoning explicit so it can be reviewed and improved.' },
